  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The numerator can be factored as\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}-8x+4=4({x}^{2}-2x+1)=4(x-1)^{2}.\n$$\n\nCanceling out any common factors that appear in the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4{x}^{2}-8x+4}{4x-4} & = \\\\ \\frac{4(x-1)^{2}}{4(x-1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{4(x-1)(x-1)}{4(x-1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{4(x-1)}(x-1)}{\\cancel{4(x-1)}} & = \\\\ \\frac{x-1}{1} & = \\\\ x-1. & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
